In future releases, I will add a patch to handle the chromosome sorting to make sure they are consistent between the 4 wig files.  Also, the chromosome naming convention (NCBI - no "chr" and UCSC - with "chr") needs to the same for all 4 wig files.  Yes, users can specify either naming convention in TITAN but at the moment, all wig files need to use the same.

Also, you should double check that the read counts in the tumour and normal wig files for chr3-chr9 do indeed have counts greater than 0.

Hope this helps.  Let me know how it turns out.

Gavin

